+# Actual UAL175 accident packet: recovered page counterpart and version comparisons
+
+October 30, 2026. **The official 237-page packet contains actual transcript pages, not just the earlier correction memoranda.** We now have a released Sector 42 page 2 of 23 counterpart, a line 1078 cover, body and footer sample, and direct comparisons with requested corrections. This advances source availability; historical accuracy, native lineage and recipient delivery remain unverified. The actual May 2003 QFR correction and 2006 administrative outcome remain separate open records.
+
+## Source and scope
+
+[Official NARA item 7598367](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7598367)  / AEA1130, [exact public PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/4-UAL-175/e-Other/4-AEA-1130-COMPLETED-ACCID-PCKG--FORMAL-ACCID-PCKG-ZNY-ARTCC-148-UAL175-REDACT-SEALED.pdf).
+
+Retrieved October 30, 2026, HTTP 200 / application/pdf, **15,505,493 bytes  / 237 physical pages**, SHA-256 `5bb71c00b716fb59425571d0c714a97a32d84b13f35dcc65d7cc6bd6f83b5179`. The entire response entity is preserved on the verified Intel store. This is an officially hosted released redacted scan, not authenticated native Word/email/audio, original signing or an exact delivered version. PDF capture dates and HTTP metadata identify different layers and are not proof when historical content changed.
+
+**Sixteen page images actually read:** 1, 2, 3, 4, 48, 49, 55, 107, 120, 148, 177, 178, 180, 186, 187, 190. **221 pages remain unread.** Visible-raster OCR followed image reading; no hidden PDF text extraction or redaction/obscurity reconstruction. No audio/listening/decoder/clock fit occurred. [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) gives exact access times, source/selected raster/OCR hashes, line counts and reused-source pins. [OBSERVATIONS.json](OBSERVATIONS.json) supplies fourteen selected field observations and the side-by-side comparison. Full scans/OCR, speech, signatures, names and contact/tracking/account data are excluded from this public derivative.
+
+The contents page has no PDF page offsets and the PDF has no standard outline/page labels. Exploratory page arithmetic was logged as a hypothesis. Some guesses were wrong: physical 178 was printed 2 of 9 and 187 was 2 of 5, not their first pages. Actual covers 177 / 186 were then read. The physical/printed mapping is a verified observation only where a page was actually viewed; unread 179 is not classified as missing, duplicate or altered.
+
+## What the actual pages add
+
+| Finding | Source locator | Supported statement and limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Published counterpart of the reported missing page** |Physical 49, printed 2 of 23; visible OCR 4, 14–16|Continued agency legend and certification text involving UAL175 are present. [The May 8 memo](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a42d0956202dacc3b971d21f479966d56fefcd60/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-package-version-chain-2026-10-30/README.md) reported this page absent from remaining packages and said two copies supplied. This locates a counterpart; it does not establish identity with those two copies, actual receipt, original signing or when the gap arose.|
+| **Requested minute labels appear in the released body** |Physical 55, printed 8 of 23; OCR 20–22|Actual rows print 1244:58/ZBW IGN and 1244:59/R42. The earlier review quoted 1245:58/1245:59 and requested 1244:58/1244:59. We retain all values. The observed snapshot is consistent with the requested replacements; it does not independently establish correct time, actual before/after edits or who changed them.|
+| **Sector 42 header/version** |Physical 48, OCR 7–21|Full Transcript; UAL175; ZNY-ARTCC-148; May 8, 2002; declared 1235–1307:58 UTC. These are printed header fields, not a certified source-clock measurement or actual delivery record.|
+| **RA55 version/page count** |Physical 107, OCR 17–26; physical 120, printed 14 of 29/OCR 5|Cover dated May 2, 2002; Full Transcript;1248–1317 UTC. A 29-page-labelled body sample is now read; earlier January/February references of 28/29 pages remain preserved. This is not a finding of when or why page count changed.|
+| **OMIC header counterpart** |Physical 148, OCR 17–26|February 4, 2002; Full Transcript; UAL175/ZNY-ARTCC-148; 1230–1344 UTC. Selected fields match the [earlier AWA940 memorandum](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/191c27f34284bdbbf006db5bb2b41071125f19d7/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-omic-memorandum-2026-10-30/README.md). The expected 26-page block is not fully read/checked. A legend entry for Huntress does not establish a timestamped communication.|
+| **TMU Departure Coordinator distinguished from line 1078** |Physical 177, header OCR 11–23; markers 43–47|May 2, 2002; 1245–1316 UTC. Markers 1245/1246/1247 requested in the earlier review now visibly appear, together with 1248/1249. Sample body pages 178/180 are printed 2/9 and 3/9. Marker presence does not prove source-audio coverage or tape-check accuracy.|
+| **Actual line 1078 cover and footer** |Physical 186, OCR 17–29, 39–40, 54;187 printed 2/5;190 printed 5/5|Cover identifies Full Transcript, January 17, 2002, UAL175/ZNY-ARTCC-148 and 1255–1316 UTC. First visible coded row is 1300:41/AD1. The final page has markers through 1316, an asterisked uncertainty note and End of Transcript. Middle pages 188/189 are unread; the exact interpreted passage and full block/source-audio continuity remain untested.|
+
+The footnote is now directly observed in a released counterpart, where the earlier correction list called for a missing asterisked note. That is stronger availability evidence than merely reporting that someone wrote Change made. It still does not date the annotation/addition or validate the transcription. The [policy crosswalk](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2e38da9806a4b3bc2550d66718831488aea76a6c/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-transcript-policy-crosswalk-2026-10-30/README.md) explains its conditional purpose; locate the marked body passage and original recording/check worksheet before evaluating it.
+
+## A concrete unresolved lineage comparison
+
+The [previously read two-page AWA937 entity](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0584407dac2190a9f9514ee157124446e60672d5/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-tmu1078-source-2026-10-30/README.md) and the packet's physical 186 share specific fields but conflict in others:
+
+| Field | AWA937 preserved observation | AEA1130 physical 186 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Date |January 17, 2002|January 17, 2002|
+| Position/range |New York TMU commercial line 1078; 1255–1316 UTC|Same selected position/range|
+| First visible timed entry |1300:41|1300:41|
+| Subject/certification aircraft |AAL11|UAL175|
+| Addressee file |ZBW-ARTCC-148|ZNY-ARTCC-148|
+
+AWA937 also retains the work-file label `UAL175_R42_memo.doc` and footer date token `09/27/2001`. None of those earlier bytes or observations was changed. The matching fields provide a testable relationship, not proof the entities share an authenticated native origin, complete text, edit history or particular delivered version. Cross-incident/template reuse, assembly and version differences remain untested alternatives. We do not select either account as controlling or infer alteration/intent from the field conflicts.
+
+This ground ATC line 1078 is separate from the flight telephone/carrier/operator evidence track. No passenger-call, billing or carrier identity is inferred from this record.
+
+## Retention label preserved as a separate lead
+
+The outer cover, physical 1 / OCR 2–6, prints ZNY-ARTCC-148, UAL175B762/E,September 11, 2001 1303 UTC and **DESTROY: March 11, 2004**. That is a printed disposition label; it does not establish actual destruction, applicable authority, or that the original file, package, recording and later scanned copy were the same retention category.
+
+The previously source-pinned [September 14 retention instruction](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/45ee3925dc1edd3137cf85182570bfc8440afcac/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-retention-directive-2026-10-30/README.md) called for retaining administrative/operational records until further notice and retaining when uncertain. Its scope and prior time ranges remain preserved. Place the cover label alongside that directive without assuming applicable withdrawal, exception, disposition or legal violation. The existence of this released scan is contrary evidence to any claim that no copy survives. It does not prove what happened to an original physical package or its recordings.
+
+Needed: actual package-versus-file retention authority, hold applicability/withdrawal records, the source copy's custody/generation, and actual disposition—not an inference from a label or metadata date. Historical directions to destroy are evidence only; no deletion was performed here.
+
+## Remaining records and tests
+
+- Inspect held but unread 188/189 for the 1078 asterisked passage and compare all five pages, plus original recording, certification/check history, native Word and source-version mapping. The footer is located; the actual interpretation remains untested.
+- Inspect OMIC 149 onward and actual endpoint/certification pages, without claiming all 26 pages from one cover. Read precise timestamps/agency changes against prior requests and obtain original source clocks/recordings through the assigned technical owner.
+- Check the complete sector 42 body/version chain, including actual requested agencies and the two historically supplied page 2 copies; obtain authenticated native enclosures and recipient acknowledgment. A current archive counterpart is not a historical delivery receipt.
+- Preserve the 29-page-labelled RA55 sample and earlier 28/29 references; inspect actual cover/end/body/annotations before explaining counts. Unread 179 must be inspected before characterizing the TMU offset pattern.
+- Keep the actual May 2003 draft/corrected QFR/delivery, signed administrative action/no-action/reasons and distinct recommendation implementation/closure outcomes open. Those are not supplied by this 2002 packet.
+
+All five tracks/eighteen substantive criteria remain partial/incomplete. Telephone flight-call native carrier/operator/call-leg fields, recorder authenticated configuration/custody/paired output/clocks, materials authenticated specimens/native measurements/calibration/same-specimen joins, and steel native preservation/transfer/inventory/attribution/selection inputs remain required. Earlier technical tests are not duplicated or relabeled missing; this packet improves record availability without substituting for empirical work.
+
+## OCR diagnostic results — failures retained
+
+The executed verifier reported **32 passing checks and four failed literal OCR anchors**. This is not an all-passed verification claim. The full result and unchanged verifier are published in VERIFICATION.json and verify_sources.py; source entity/hash/page count, selected OCR hashes/line counts and scoped locators passed.
+
+| Physical page | Preserved OCR observation | Image reading / failed expectation |
+|---|---|---|
+|49|`Page 2 Of 23`|The predicate expected lowercase `of`; capitalization differs.|
+|186|First-row code `ADI`|Manual image/legend reading is `AD1`.|
+|187|`Page 2 of S`|Manual image reading is `Page 2 of 5`.|
+|190|`Page 5 of S`|Manual image reading is `Page 5 of 5`.|
+
+These processing observations and the original images remain separate. No OCR/source bytes were edited to obtain a pass, no failed criterion was hidden, and the unchanged checker will reproduce those failures with the pinned inputs. The manual observations are image-based and source-linked; they are not independent authentication of voices, clock time or delivery. A later OCR-method improvement remains optional TODO work and would retain these originals and failures. Publication-byte verification is a separate test.
+
+## Accountability and verification
+
+| Requirement | Outcome | Limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| Acquire primary operational records |Whole 237-page released PDF pinned/preserved; 16 selected images read |221 unread; official hosting is not native or historical accuracy authentication.|
+| Preserve conflicting values and sources |Selected field ledger, source links, prior snapshots and side-by-side table |No value reconciled, preferred, normalized or cause/intent inferred.|
+| Leave missing inputs as TODOs |Counterpart/footnote availability updated; exact unperformed tests and receipt/media/native joins above |No eighteen-item criterion closed; prior dated statuses preserved.|
+| Exact revision diff |[TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff), new dated additive unit against absent-file baseline |Separate from visual reading; earlier records unchanged.|
+| Publish eligible material as AveLyra |Safe notes/pins/selected fields/verification only |No raw scans/OCR/speech/personnel/contact/signature/tracking/account/private-case payload. Separate publication receipt verifies identity/ref/all bodies.|
+
+The verifier checks the exact source entity/page count, selected visible OCR hashes/line spans and safe field anchors. It does not validate the original voices, clock, completeness, interpretation, signing, delivered version, compliance, intent or independence. No outreach, new request/fee/filing, private push, source overwrite/deletion or history rewrite occurred. Publication does not complete the substantive goal.
